, CI passed, and PR #101 is open against main with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **The bug:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` said in its description that it used banker's rounding (FIN-212), but the code actually rounded halves up. That's why `2.665` came out as `2.67` instead of the `2.66` the test expects.\n- **The fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-round-half-even`, I changed the rounding mode to banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`).\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on commit `08d3cd5986`.\n- **PR #101:** The request to open the PR timed out, but the PR had been created anyway. I checked the open PRs before trying again, so there's no duplicate. It was missing the reviewer, so I added alex separately.\n\nI couldn't look up FIN-212 because the advisory tool didn't recognise it. The change follows the test and the existing description in the code.\n\nI haven't merged it. Merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01HCavc4NNRkyd6kVjfKqD9A", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01WbEDZQ16rxiV38mnPPUs1x", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_013yHYCZRZWidyju9FdxQj96", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212"}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01LR4kwyZPTJHv5yGW5riRdN", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-round-half-even"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01HZg5bNaMYNv2nMJjgxMK6Z", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-round-half-even", "message": "Use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) in round_money per FIN-212", "fi